__init__.py            \\u2190 7 tool classes + mount() entrypoint (~957 lines)\\n\\u2502   \\u2502\\n\\u2502   
\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 tool-lnd/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 pyproject.toml             \\u2190 Package 
config for lnd module\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 amplifier_module_tool_lnd/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502       
\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 __init__.py            \\u2190 6 tool classes + mount() entrypoint (~487 lines)\\n\\u2502   
\\u2502\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 tool-aggeus-markets/\\n\\u2502       \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 pyproject.toml    
\\u2190 Package config for aggeus module\\n\\u2502       \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 
amplifier_module_tool_aggeus_markets/\\n\\u2502           \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 __init__.py            \\u2190 4 tool 
classes + Nostr helpers + mount() (~629 lines)\\n\\u2502\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 tests/\\n\\u2502   
\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 conftest.py                    \\u2190 Stub amplifier_core for testing without 
framework\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 test_split_utxos.py            \\u2190 2 async tests for 
SplitUtxosTool\\n\\u2502\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 docs/\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 plans/                        
\\u2190 Empty directory (plans lived here during dev)\\n\\u2502\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 .env.example                   
\\u2190 Template for all environment variables\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 .gitignore                         \\u2190 
Standard ignores + .amplifier/, .venv/\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 .claude/settings.local.json        \\u2190 Local Claude 
tool permissions (docker, python, ls)\\n\\u2502\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 .venv/                             \\u2190 
Virtual env (Python 3.11 + 3.12 both present)\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 .pytest_cache/                     \\u2190 Test 
cache\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 .ruff_cache/                       \\u2190 Linting cache\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 1. 
Bundle Configuration \\u2014 `bundle.md`\\n\\n**Path:** `bundle.md`\\n\\nThis is the Amplifier bundle manifest, using 
YAML frontmatter fenced by `---`:\\n\\n```yaml\\nbundle:\\n  name: utxo-bundle\\n  version: 0.1.0\\n  description: 
Bitcoin UTXO manager \\u2014 inspect, split, and manage wallets via Bitcoin Core RPC\\n\\nincludes:\\n  - bundle: 
git+https://github.com/microsoft/amplifier-foundation@main\\n\\ntools:\\n  - module: tool-bitcoin-rpc\\n    source: 
./modules/tool-bitcoin-rpc\\n    config:\\n      rpc_host: 127.0.0.1\\n      rpc_port: 18445        # regtest default 
port\\n\\n  - module: tool-lnd\\n    source: ./modules/tool-lnd\\n    config:\\n      rest_host: 127.0.0.1\\n      
rest_port: 8085\\n\\n  - module: tool-aggeus-markets\\n    source: ./modules/tool-aggeus-markets\\n    config:\\n      
relay_host: localhost\\n      relay_port: 8080\\n      coordinator_pubkey: b49e3064...   # embedded in every market 
listing\\n```\\n\\nAfter the frontmatter, the body includes:\\n- `@utxo-bundle:context/instructions.md` \\u2014 injects
the AI instructions\\n- `@foundation:context/shared/common-system-base.md` \\u2014 injects shared Amplifier foundation 
context\\n\\n**Key design decision:** Defaults all ports to `regtest` configuration (18445, 8085, 8080), meaning this 
bundle is designed for **local development/testing** against a Polar-style Bitcoin network stack.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 2. 
Context File \\u2014 `context/instructions.md`\\n\\n**Path:** `context/instructions.md`\\n\\nThis is the AI's 
behavioral contract \\u2014 it tells the agent exactly how to use each tool and how to translate natural language into 
tool calls. Organized into four sections:\\n\\n| Section | Tools Covered | Key Behaviors 
|\\n|---------|--------------|---------------|\\n| **UTXO Management** | `list_utxos`, `split_utxos`, `manage_wallet`, 
`consolidate_utxos`, `mine_blocks`, `generate_address` | Present UTXO table verbatim in code fences; translate \\\"6 
UTXOs: 2@2k, 2@4k, 2@8k\\\" to `outputs` array; mine 101 blocks for spendable funds |\\n| **Lightning (LND)** | 
`lnd_create_invoice`, `lnd_list_invoices`, `lnd_lookup_invoice`, `lnd_pay_invoice`, `lnd_get_node_info`, 
`lnd_channel_balance` | All `lnd_*` tools auto-connect, no credentials needed from user; show full BOLT11 string after 
creation |\\n| **Aggeus Markets** | `aggeus_list_markets`, `aggeus_get_market`, `aggeus_list_shares`, 
`aggeus_create_market` | Extract market questions as yes/no; warn user to save preimages immediately |\\n| **Wallet 
workflow** | `manage_wallet` | Use `list` first when user says \\\"my wallet\\\" without specifying a name 
|\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 3. Module 1: `tool-bitcoin-rpc`\\n\\n**Path:** `modules/tool-bitcoin-rpc/`  \\n**Package:** 
`amplifier-module-tool-bitcoin-rpc` v0.1.0  \\n**Dependency:** `httpx>=0.27`  \\n**Entry point:** 
`amplifier_module_tool_bitcoin_rpc:mount`\\n\\n#### Tools (7 total)\\n\\n| Tool Class | Tool Name | What It Does 
|\\n|------------|-----------|-------------|\\n| `ListUtxosTool` | `list_utxos` | Calls `listunspent` RPC; returns a 
markdown table sorted by address with sats, BTC, confirmations, outpoint |\\n| `SplitUtxosTool` | `split_utxos` | 
Splits wallet funds into N discrete UTXOs. Uses raw tx pipeline: `createrawtransaction \\u2192 fundrawtransaction 
\\u2192 signrawtransactionwithwallet \\u2192 sendrawtransaction` to bypass Bitcoin Core's duplicate-address rejection 
|\\n| `ManageWalletTool` | `manage_wallet` | 5 actions: `list`, `info`, `create`, `load`, `unload`. Wraps 
`listwallets`, `listwalletdir`, `getwalletinfo`, `createwallet`, `loadwallet`, `unloadwallet` |\\n| 
`GenerateAddressTool` | `generate_address` | Calls `getnewaddress`; supports `bech32`, `bech32m`, `p2sh-segwit`, 
`legacy` types |\\n| `SendCoinsTool` | `send_coins` | Calls `sendtoaddress`; accepts sats, optional memo, optional 
`subtract_fee_from_amount` |\\n| `ConsolidateUtxosTool` | `consolidate_utxos` | Sweeps multiple UTXOs into one output. 
Filters by `min_confirmations`, `max_amount_sats`, `min_amount_sats`, or explicit outpoints. Uses `sendall` RPC 
(fee-from-output, no change) |\\n| `MineBlocksTool` | `mine_blocks` | Calls `generatetoaddress`; warns if <101 blocks 
(coinbase maturity); regtest/signet only |\\n\\n#### Credential resolution (`_load_credentials`)\\n1. Check 
`BITCOIN_COOKIE_FILE` (preferred for local nodes \\u2014 reads `user:pass` from the cookie file)\\n2. Fall back to 
`BITCOIN_RPC_USER` / `BITCOIN_RPC_PASSWORD` env vars\\n\\n#### RPC URL pattern\\nAll wallet-scoped calls use 
`http://{host}:{port}/wallet/{name}` automatically.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 4. Module 2: `tool-lnd`\\n\\n**Path:** 
`modules/tool-lnd/`  \\n**Package:** `amplifier-module-tool-lnd` v0.1.0  \\n**Dependencies:** none (re-uses httpx from 
the venv)  \\n**Entry point:** `amplifier_module_tool_lnd:mount`\\n\\n#### Tools (6 total)\\n\\n| Tool Class | Tool 
Name | API Endpoint | What It Does |\\n|------------|-----------|-------------|-------------|\\n| `CreateInvoiceTool` |
`lnd_create_invoice` | `POST /v1/invoices` | Creates BOLT11 invoice; supports fixed or any-amount; returns 
payment_request + r_hash |\\n| `ListInvoicesTool` | `lnd_list_invoices` | `GET /v1/invoices` | Lists invoices in a 
markdown table; `pending_only` filter; maps state strings to human labels |\\n| `LookupInvoiceTool` | 
`lnd_lookup_invoice` | `GET /v1/invoice/{r_hash}` | Looks up a specific invoice by hex payment hash |\\n| 
`NodeInfoTool` | `lnd_get_node_info` | `GET /v1/getinfo` | Shows alias, pubkey, version, block height, active channels,
peers, sync status |\\n| `ChannelBalanceTool` | `lnd_channel_balance` | `GET /v1/balance/channels` | Local (sendable) 
and remote (receivable) balances + pending |\\n| `PayInvoiceTool` | `lnd_pay_invoice` | `POST 
/v1/channels/transactions` | Pays BOLT11 synchronously (`SendPaymentSync`); configurable fee limit and timeout; returns
preimage on success |\\n\\n#### Authentication\\n- TLS cert path: `LND_TLS_CERT` env var (required)\\n- Macaroon: 
`LND_MACAROON_PATH` \\u2014 file is read and hex-encoded, sent as `Grpc-Metadata-Macaroon` header\\n- Both are required
at mount time; `ValueError` raised if missing\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 5. Module 3: `tool-aggeus-markets`\\n\\n**Path:** 
`modules/tool-aggeus-markets/`  \\n**Package:** `amplifier-module-tool-aggeus-markets` v0.1.0  \\n**Dependencies:** 
`websockets>=12.0`, `coincurve>=13.0`, `cryptography>=42.0`  \\n**Entry point:** 
`amplifier_module_tool_aggeus_markets:mount`\\n\\nAggeus is a Bitcoin-native prediction market protocol on Nostr + 
Lightning. This module implements the protocol client side.\\n\\n#### Protocol 
constants\\n```python\\nAGGEUS_MARKET_LISTING_KIND = 46416  # kind for market_definition events\\nAGGEUS_SHARE_KIND = 
46415           # kind for share announcements\\nPROTOCOL_VERSION = 1\\n```\\n\\n#### Nostr wire helpers (private)\\n- 
`_query_relay(relay_url, filters, timeout)` \\u2014 sends `REQ` subscription, collects events until `EOSE`\\n- 
`_publish_event(relay_url, event, timeout)` \\u2014 sends `EVENT`, waits for `OK` acknowledgment\\n- 
`_nostr_event_id(...)` \\u2014 SHA256 of NIP-01 canonical commitment array\\n- `_derive_pubkey(privkey_hex)` \\u2014 
BIP340 x-only public key via `coincurve`\\n- `_schnorr_sign(privkey_hex, event_id_hex)` \\u2014 BIP340 Schnorr 
signature via `coincurve`\\n- `_build_signed_event(...)` \\u2014 assembles complete signed Nostr event dict\\n- 
`_parse_market(event)` \\u2014 parses kind-46416 content into structured dict (MarketShareableData layout: 
``)\\n\\n#### Tools (3 always + 1 conditional)\\n\\n| Tool Class | Tool Name | What It Does 
|\\n|------------|-----------|-------------|\\n| `ListMarketsTool` | `aggeus_list_markets` | Queries kind-46416 events 
with `#t: market_definition` tag; returns table with name, shortened ID, oracle, resolution block |\\n| `GetMarketTool`
| `aggeus_get_market` | Queries by `#d` tag (market_id); shows full protocol fields including yes/no hashes, relay list
|\\n| `ListSharesTool` | `aggeus_list_shares` | Queries kind-46415 events by `#e` (market_id); calculates buyer cost as
`(100 - confidence%) * 100 sats` |\\n| `CreateMarketTool` | `aggeus_create_market` | **Conditional** \\u2014 only 
mounted when `oracle_private_key` + `coordinator_pubkey` are configured. Generates random preimages, SHA256-hashes 
them, builds and signs a kind-46416 event, publishes to relay |\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 6. Tests \\u2014 
`tests/`\\n\\n**Path:** `tests/`\\n\\n| File | Purpose |\\n|------|---------|\\n| `conftest.py` | Stubs out 
`amplifier_core` (`ModuleCoordinator` + `ToolResult`) so tests run without the full Amplifier framework installed |\\n|
`test_split_utxos.py` | 2 async tests using `pytest-asyncio` + `respx` for HTTP mocking |\\n\\n**Test coverage:**\\n- 
`test_rpc_call_getnewaddress` \\u2014 verifies `_rpc_call` correctly POSTs and returns the `result` field\\n- 
`test_split_utxos_basic` \\u2014 verifies end-to-end `execute()` flow: mocks `getnewaddress` (3 times) and `send`, 
checks txid + all UTXOs appear in output\\n\\n**Note:** The test `test_split_utxos_basic` mocks the `send` method but 
the actual implementation uses `createrawtransaction \\u2192 fundrawtransaction \\u2192 signrawtransactionwithwallet 
\\u2192 sendrawtransaction`. The test is slightly **out of sync** with the current implementation (the test checks for 
a `send` call that no longer exists).\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 7. Package Configuration\\n\\n#### 
`modules/tool-bitcoin-rpc/pyproject.toml`\\n```toml\\nname = \\\"amplifier-module-tool-bitcoin-rpc\\\"\\nversion = 
