      "type": "text",
      "text": "\n\nGood call -- the foundation expert suggested a **wallet-operator** as a separate agent from UTXO 
analysis. Let me think about the scope split here before writing.\n\nLooking at your 7 Bitcoin RPC tools, there are two
natural groupings:\n\n| Concern | Tools | Focus |\n|---------|-------|-------|\n| **UTXO operations** (already in 
utxo-manager) | `list_utxos`, `split_utxos`, `consolidate_utxos`, `send_coins` | Inspecting and moving funds that 
already exist |\n| **Wallet lifecycle + environment** | `manage_wallet`, `generate_address`, `mine_blocks` | Setting up
wallets, generating addresses, advancing the chain |\n\nBut there's real overlap -- `split_utxos` needs a wallet 
context, `mine_blocks` is how you fund a wallet but also how you confirm a split. The utxo-manager already covers all 7
tools.\n\nA few directions we could take:\n\n**Option A: wallet-operator as a separate, focused agent**\nOwns 
`manage_wallet`, `generate_address`, `mine_blocks`. Handles the \"infrastructure\" side -- creating wallets, funding 
them, confirming transactions. The utxo-manager then focuses purely on UTXO inspection and manipulation (list, split, 
consolidate, send). Clean separation, but requires cross-delegation when the user says \"set up a wallet and split some
UTXOs.\"\n\n**Option B: wallet-operator as an orchestration agent**\nDoesn't own tools directly -- instead it delegates
to utxo-manager for the actual RPC calls but owns the *workflows* (e.g., \"set up Alice and Bob with funded wallets and
a channel between them\"). More of a scenario runner.\n\n**Option C: Keep utxo-manager as the single Bitcoin L1 agent, 
add wallet-operator later**\nSince all 7 tools are tightly coupled to Bitcoin Core RPC, one agent covers them well. The
wallet-operator becomes valuable when you have multi-wallet or multi-node scenarios.\n\nWhat's your instinct? Do you 
see the wallet lifecycle as distinct enough to warrant its own agent now, or would you rather keep utxo-manager as the 
comprehensive Bitcoin L1 agent and focus the next agent on Lightning or Aggeus instead?"
    }
  ],
  "metadata": {
    "timestamp": "2026-02-26T21:39:59.839+00:00"
  }
}
