`generate_address` | Derive a new receive address (`bech32`, `bech32m`, `p2sh-segwit`, `legacy`) |\\n    85\\t| 
`send_coins` | Send sats to an address via `sendtoaddress` |\\n    86\\t| `mine_blocks` | Mine regtest/signet blocks 
and direct coinbase reward to an address |\\n    87\\t\\n    88\\t---\\n    89\\t\\n    90\\t## Core Workflows\\n    
91\\t\\n    92\\t### Inspect the UTXO Set\\n    93\\t\\n    94\\t**Always start with `list_utxos`** before any 
operation that depends on wallet state.\\n    95\\t\\n    96\\t1. Call `list_utxos` with the target wallet\\n    
97\\t2. Present the table output verbatim inside a code fence -- never reformat or omit rows\\n    98\\t3. Summarize: 
count, total sats, largest/smallest, dust count\\n    99\\t\\n   100\\t### Split UTXOs\\n   101\\t\\n   102\\tTranslate
natural language into the `outputs` array:\\n   103\\t\\n   104\\t- \\\"6 UTXOs: 2 at 2k, 2 at 4k, 2 at 8k\\\" 
becomes:\\n   105\\t  ```json\\n   106\\t  {\\\"outputs\\\": [\\n   107\\t    {\\\"amount_sats\\\": 2000, 
\\\"count\\\": 2},\\n   108\\t    {\\\"amount_sats\\\": 4000, \\\"count\\\": 2},\\n   109\\t    {\\\"amount_sats\\\": 
8000, \\\"count\\\": 2}\\n   110\\t  ]}\\n   111\\t  ```\\n   112\\t- If the user provides an external address, pass it
as `address`\\n   113\\t- Otherwise a new wallet address is generated automatically\\n   114\\t- After success: report 
the txid and list of created outputs\\n   115\\t- Remind: transaction needs confirmation (mine a block) before new 
