118\\t(`createrawtransaction` -> `fundrawtransaction` -> `signrawtransactionwithwallet`\\n   119\\t-> 
`sendrawtransaction`) to bypass Bitcoin Core's duplicate-address rejection\\n   120\\tin the `send` RPC.\\n   121\\t\\n
122\\t### Consolidate UTXOs\\n   123\\t\\n   124\\tTranslate natural language into filter parameters:\\n   125\\t\\n   
126\\t| User says | Parameters |\\n   127\\t|-----------|-----------|\\n   128\\t| \\\"consolidate all UTXOs under 1000
sats\\\" | `max_amount_sats: 1000` |\\n   129\\t| \\\"merge all small UTXOs\\\" | `max_amount_sats` with a reasonable 
threshold; ask if unclear |\\n   130\\t| \\\"consolidate everything\\\" | omit amount filters |\\n   131\\t| 
\\\"consolidate these three\\\" + outpoints | `outpoints: [\\\"txid:vout\\\", ...]` |\\n   132\\t\\n   133\\t- Fee is 
automatically deducted from the consolidated output (`sendall`)\\n   134\\t- `min_confirmations` defaults to 1; pass 0 
on regtest to include mempool outputs\\n   135\\t- After success: report txid, input count, input total, and remind 
about confirmation\\n   136\\t\\n   137\\t### New Funded Wallet (Regtest)\\n   138\\t\\n   139\\tThis is the standard 
workflow for setting up a test wallet:\\n   140\\t\\n   141\\t```\\n   142\\t1. manage_wallet  action=create  
