Confirm a Pending Transaction\\n   151\\t\\n   152\\t```\\n   153\\tmine_blocks  num_blocks=1  address=<any address>\\n
154\\t```\\n   155\\t\\n   156\\tUse 1 block for speed in regtest. Bitcoin Core considers 6 confirmations 
\\\"final\\\"\\n   157\\tbut 1 is sufficient for most test workflows.\\n   158\\t\\n   159\\t### Send Funds\\n   
160\\t\\n   161\\t- `send_coins` uses `sendtoaddress` -- the wallet selects inputs automatically\\n   162\\t- Amount is
in satoshis\\n   163\\t- Set `subtract_fee_from_amount: true` if the recipient should receive exactly\\n   164\\t  the 
specified amount minus fee\\n   165\\t- After success: report txid and amount sent\\n   166\\t\\n   167\\t### Wallet 
Inventory\\n   168\\t\\n   169\\tWhen the user says \\\"my wallet\\\" without specifying a name, call\\n   
170\\t`manage_wallet action=list` first to show what's available.\\n   171\\t\\n   172\\t---\\n   173\\t\\n   174\\t## 
UTXO Health Heuristics\\n   175\\t\\n   176\\tUse these when analyzing the UTXO set:\\n   177\\t\\n   178\\t| Category 
| Threshold | Guidance |\\n   179\\t|----------|-----------|----------|\\n   180\\t| **Dust** | < 546 sats | 
Economically unspendable at normal fee rates |\\n   181\\t| **Small** | < 1,000 sats | Marginally spendable; candidate 
for consolidation |\\n   182\\t| **Fragmented** | > 20 UTXOs at same address | Privacy and fee concern |\\n   183\\t| 
**Consolidation trigger** | Fee to spend UTXO > 30% of its value | Consolidation saves money long-term |\\n   184\\t\\n
185\\tWhen presenting analysis, include these categories with counts so the user\\n   186\\tcan make informed 
