{
  "role": "tool",
  "name": "delegate",
  "tool_call_id": "toolu_01259raCWMmx8jra2RXkRL9S",
  "content": "{\"response\": \"Now I have everything needed to give you the authoritative answer. The BUNDLE_GUIDE.md 
has a direct, explicit section for exactly this situation. Let me break it down.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Config in Behavior 
YAML vs. Environment Variables\\n\\n### The Authoritative Section: \\\"App-Level Runtime 
Injection\\\"\\n\\nBUNDLE_GUIDE.md lines 982\\u20131024 answer all four questions directly:\\n\\n> **Don't declare in 
bundles:**\\n> - Provider API keys or model preferences \\u2192 App injects from settings\\n> - **Environment-specific 
paths \\u2192 App injects via tool config** \\u2190 this is you\\n> - User preferences \\u2192 App handles them\\n>\\n>
**This enables:**\\n> - Same bundle works across environments\\n> - Secrets stay out of version control\\n> - Apps can 
restrict/expand tool capabilities per context\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Q1: Should the behavior YAML have config values if 
modules already read env vars?\\n\\n**No.** The values you have hardcoded are every one of the things the guide says to
keep out of bundles:\\n\\n```yaml\\n# \\u274c ALL of these are environment-specific \\u2014 wrong layer\\nconfig:\\n  
rpc_host: 127.0.0.1       # Polar-specific\\n  rpc_port: 18445            # regtest-specific port\\n  rest_host: 
127.0.0.1       # local-only\\n  rest_port: 8080\\n  relay_host: localhost\\n  relay_port: 8080\\n  coordinator_pubkey:
b49e30...  # instance-specific, possibly sensitive\\n```\\n\\nYour modules already do the right thing by reading env 
vars as fallbacks. The behavior YAML config is **fighting against** that design \\u2014 it creates a hardcoded middle 
layer between the module's env-var logic and the user's actual environment.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Q2: Correct pattern for 
environment-varying config (dev vs. staging vs. different Polar setups)?\\n\\n**`~/.amplifier/settings.yaml` (or a 
project-local `.amplifier/settings.yaml`).** The guide shows this explicitly:\\n\\n```yaml\\n# 
~/.amplifier/settings.yaml  \\u2190 per-environment, per-user, gitignored\\nmodules:\\n  tools:\\n    - module: 
tool-bitcoin-rpc\\n      config:\\n        rpc_host: 127.0.0.1\\n        rpc_port: 18445\\n        cookie_file: 
/path/to/.bitcoin/regtest/.cookie\\n\\n    - module: tool-lnd\\n      config:\\n        rest_host: 127.0.0.1\\n        
rest_port: 8080\\n        tls_cert: /path/to/tls.cert\\n        macaroon_path: /path/to/admin.macaroon\\n\\n    - 
module: tool-aggeus-markets\\n      config:\\n        relay_host: localhost\\n        relay_port: 8080\\n        
coordinator_pubkey: b49e3064...\\n```\\n\\nFrom the guide:\\n> Tool configs are **deep-merged by module ID** \\u2014 
your settings extend the bundle's config, not replace it.\\n\\nSo each Polar setup, staging env, or dev machine gets 
its own `settings.yaml`. The bundle stays identical across all of them.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Q3: Can behavior YAML config 
values reference environment variables?\\n\\nThe guide shows `${VAR}` interpolation **in `settings.yaml`** for 
providers:\\n\\n```yaml\\n# settings.yaml \\u2014 ${} interpolation is documented here\\nproviders:\\n  - module: 
provider-anthropic\\n    config:\\n      api_key: ${ANTHROPIC_API_KEY}\\n```\\n\\n**The guide does not document 
`${VAR}` interpolation in behavior YAML tool config.** More importantly, it's the wrong question \\u2014 if your 
modules already read from env vars natively, there's no need for interpolation anywhere in YAML. The module is the 
right place for that logic, and yours already have it.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Q4: Recommended approach \\u2014 strip the 
config block entirely?\\n\\n**Yes. Strip it.** Here's what your behavior file should look like:\\n\\n```yaml\\n# 
behaviors/utxo-bundle.yaml\\nbundle:\\n  name: utxo-bundle-behavior\\n  version: 0.1.0\\n  description: >\\n    Bitcoin
Core wallet management, Lightning Network, and Aggeus prediction\\n    markets \\u2014 tools, agents, and context for a
local development stack.\\n\\ntools:\\n  - module: tool-bitcoin-rpc\\n    source: ../modules/tool-bitcoin-rpc\\n    # 
Config resolved from env: BITCOIN_COOKIE_FILE, BITCOIN_RPC_HOST, BITCOIN_RPC_PORT\\n\\n  - module: tool-lnd\\n    
source: ../modules/tool-lnd\\n    # Config resolved from env: LND_REST_HOST, LND_REST_PORT, LND_TLS_CERT, 
LND_MACAROON_PATH\\n\\n  - module: tool-aggeus-markets\\n    source: ../modules/tool-aggeus-markets\\n    # Config 
resolved from env: AGGEUS_RELAY_URL, AGGEUS_ORACLE_PRIVKEY, AGGEUS_COORDINATOR_PUBKEY\\n\\nagents:\\n  include:\\n    -
utxo-bundle:wallet-manager\\n    - utxo-bundle:lightning-specialist\\n    - utxo-bundle:market-maker\\n\\ncontext:\\n  
include:\\n    - utxo-bundle:context/instructions.md\\n    - utxo-bundle:context/aggeus-protocol.md\\n```\\n\\nAnd ship
a `settings.example.yaml` in the repo that users copy and fill in:\\n\\n```yaml\\n# settings.example.yaml \\u2014 copy 
to ~/.amplifier/settings.yaml and fill in your values\\nmodules:\\n  tools:\\n    - module: tool-bitcoin-rpc\\n      
config:\\n        rpc_host: 127.0.0.1\\n        rpc_port: 18445          # 18443 mainnet, 18444 testnet, 18445 
regtest\\n        cookie_file: ~/.bitcoin/regtest/.cookie\\n\\n    - module: tool-lnd\\n      config:\\n        
rest_host: 127.0.0.1\\n        rest_port: 8080\\n        tls_cert: ~/.lnd/tls.cert\\n        macaroon_path: 
~/.lnd/data/chain/bitcoin/regtest/admin.macaroon\\n\\n    - module: tool-aggeus-markets\\n      config:\\n        
